    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That \"minefield\" comparison is pretty intense. If we're looking at this from a purely structural perspective, is it fair to say that these multi-ethnic societies in these specific regions are fundamentally less capable of maintaining order compared to more ethnically unified nations? I'm trying to understand if the instability is just a political hurdle, or if it's more of an inherent characteristic of these specific types of demographic compositions.",
